Subject: [PATCH] pvrsgx 1.6: dump BIF directory-list base at hardware recovery

SGX530 selects one active page directory through EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0.
On a BIF page fault the microkernel raises hardware recovery; HWRecoveryResetSGX
calls SGXDumpDebugInfo before SGXReset reprograms that register with the BIF
reset PD. The existing dump records the fault address but not the directory that
was active when it faulted, so the log cannot show which memory context the GPU
was using.

Dump EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0 in that pre-reset register block, alongside the
kernel and BIF-reset page-directory device addresses shifted into BASE0 units,
so the captured base decodes as the kernel PD, the reset PD, or a client PD.

Also log the page-directory device address in MMU_Finalise. A client context
destroyed while SGX or recovery still selects its directory would show a
finalized PD whose BASE0 matches the active directory-list base -- the
prediction under investigation for the 0F0AB000 / 000D0000 / 000E5000 fault
cascade preceding the PVRSRVProcessQueues teardown Oops.

Diagnostic only: two log statements on the recovery and context-teardown paths,
no behavioural change. Remove once the faulting directory is identified.
---
 .../gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/mmu.c    | 4 ++++
 .../drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c    | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/mmu.c
index e7d19fe3b..79ce3416a 100755
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/mmu.c
@@ -1324,0 +1325,4 @@ MMU_Finalise (MMU_CONTEXT *psMMUContext)
+	PVR_LOG(("MMU_Finalise: freeing MMU context 0x%08X PD=0x%08X (BASE0=0x%08X)",
+			(IMG_UINTPTR_T)psMMUContext,
+			psMMUContext->sPDDevPAddr.uiAddr,
+			psMMUContext->sPDDevPAddr.uiAddr >> EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0_ADDR_SHIFT));
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
index 8b12979ee..3f348c4f8 100755
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
@@ -971,0 +972 @@ static IMG_VOID SGXDumpDebugInfo (PVRSRV_SGXDEV_INFO	*psDevInfo,
+			SGXDumpDebugReg(psDevInfo, ui32CoreNum, "EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0: ", EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0);
@@ -976,0 +978,5 @@ static IMG_VOID SGXDumpDebugInfo (PVRSRV_SGXDEV_INFO	*psDevInfo,
+		PVR_LOG(("SGX PD refs: kernel BASE0=0x%08X reset BASE0=0x%08X (kernelPD=0x%08X resetPD=0x%08X)",
+					psDevInfo->sKernelPDDevPAddr.uiAddr >> EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0_ADDR_SHIFT,
+					psDevInfo->sBIFResetPDDevPAddr.uiAddr >> EUR_CR_BIF_DIR_LIST_BASE0_ADDR_SHIFT,
+					psDevInfo->sKernelPDDevPAddr.uiAddr,
+					psDevInfo->sBIFResetPDDevPAddr.uiAddr));
